issue.body:
Apparently the set_rate command isn't working as it ought to against ArduPilot. This came up in https://discord.com/channels/1022170275984457759/1022185801615933460/threads/1453074335584485566.

Code sample to check:

```
_telemetry->set_rate_position_async(10.0, [](mavsdk::Telemetry::Result result) {
        if (result != mavsdk::Telemetry::Result::Success) {
            std::cerr << "Failed to set telemetry position rate" << std::endl;
        }
    });

    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));

    _telemetry->set_rate_attitude_euler_async(10.0, [](mavsdk::Telemetry::Result result) {
        if (result != mavsdk::Telemetry::Result::Success) {
            std::cerr << "Failed to set drone euler rate" << std::endl;
        }
    });

    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
```
